// tsx/typescript-04: a Vitest test's mode option as @vitest/eslint-plugin (1.6) reads it, for no-disabled-tests
// and no-focused-tests of batch typescript-04.
//
// What a rule gets from this library:
//   set_mode_option(c, x, k)  test or suite c's options object (its second argument) sets mode x (only, skip):
//                             its last `x` property is `x: true`, k that property's key
//
// Examples:
//   no-focused-tests:   test("t", { only: true }, fn)                  set_mode_option(c, "only", only)
//                       test("t", { only: true, only() {} }, fn)       none: the method is the last only
//   no-disabled-tests:  test("t", { skip: true }, fn)                  set_mode_option(c, "skip", skip)
//                       test("t", { skip: true, get skip() {…} }, fn)  none: the getter is the last skip
//
// The plugin's findVitestModeProperty takes the last Property whose key is the mode's name (`x: v`, `x() {}`,
// `get x() {}`, `set x(v) {}`, the shorthand `{ x }`; a spread is no Property) and wants its value the literal
// true. tsx/ts-b-vitest's mode_option says the same, but finds "last" by `earlier`, which has no rows under
// run-policies: there every `x: true` counted. The properties of one object are siblings, so "last" here is: no
// later sibling has the name, by `precedes`.
//
// Builds on tsx/ts-b-vitest (mode_option, option_entry) and core.
#include "tsx/ts-b-vitest.rerail"

.decl set_mode_option(c: node, x: symbol, k: node)
set_mode_option(c, x, k) :- mode_option(c, x, k), child(e, k, _), child(o, e, _), !later_mode_key(o, e, x).
// later_mode_key(o, e, x): a property of o after e is named x.
.decl later_mode_key(o: node, e: node, x: symbol)
later_mode_key(o, e, x) :- mode_option(_, x, k), child(e, k, _), child(o, e, _), option_entry(o, f, x, _), precedes(e, f).
later_mode_key(o, e, x) :- mode_option(_, x, k), child(e, k, _), child(o, e, _), child(o, f, _),
    kind(f, "shorthand_property_identifier"), text(f, x), precedes(e, f).
